  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Supporting Pacific Genetic Diversity for Climate Resilient Agriculture</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This investment supports the implementation of the business plan (second phase) of the Centre for Pacific Crops and Trees (CePaCT) over the period 2024-2028. CePaCT, as the Pacific&#x2019;s only regional genebank and established by the Pacific Community (SPC), plays a crucial role in leveraging the unique biodiversity of the Pacific to enhance food and nutrition security and build resilience against the increasing variability of climate change for SPC members. This investment supports CePaCT meet international genebank standards and excellence; strengthen germplasm security and diversity for climate adaptation and enhanced climate resilience; and facilitate access, collaboration, and target community impact and resilience to the impacts of climate change.</narrative>
  </description>
